factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The article says the price of 'இளநீர்' (tender coconut water) fell by Rs.2 and is fixed at Rs.42, and does not say it is per piece; the draft writes 'ஒன்று ரூ.42' (one piece costs Rs.42), though the article says 'தரமான குட்டை, நெட்டை, வீரிய ஒட்டு இளநீர் விலை... 42 ரூபாயாக' which is ambiguous, and the reel_script and slides present it as a per-unit price 'ஒன்று' not stated in the article
  The article says the spotty husk is caused by Eriophyid mite damage ('ஈயோபைட்'/ஈரியோபைட்), but the draft says the husk becomes rough 'ஈரியோபைட் பூச்சி தாக்குதலால்' as a cause, which matches; however the caption and reel_script also state the price drop is caused by the rain-related demand fall combined with the husk problem as a single cause, mixing two separate causes (cold-season demand drop and husk damage) into one sentence
  The reel_script omits the article's point that vendors demand lower prices specifically because of the rough husk: it does say this, but the slide 'வியாபாரிகளின் நிலை' line 'சொரசொரப்பால் வியாபாரிகள் விலையைக் குறைத்துக் கேட்கின்றனர்' is fine; the caption's 'ℹ️ மக்கள் கவனத்திற்கு: தரமான இளநீருக்கு நல்ல விலை கிடைக்கிறது' presents a consumer-directed message that the article does not state as a warning to the public
