  reel_script says the Hindu groups' protest was against the ban but the article attributes the place to 'அங்கலக்குறிச்சி' in headline while the reel_script claims the temple is in அங்கலக்குறிச்சி; the article says the temple is near அங்கலக்குறிச்சி, so this is a slight location mismatch
  reel_script says 'ஆனைமலை புலிகள் காப்பகம் அருகே' while article says the temple is inside the Anaimalai Tiger Reserve forest area (near அங்கலக்குறிச்சி), not 'near' it
  slides_spec and reel_script state the ban was announced 'நேற்று' - the article says 'நேற்று' so this is correct, but slides_spec line 'பக்தர்கள் மலை கோவிலுக்கு செல்ல அனுமதி இல்லை' omits that the ban is for non-local people in the verification section, creating a contradiction with the 'உள்ளூர் மக்களுக்கு மட்டும் அனுமதி' point
  reel_script says 'பொதுமக்களின் பாதுகாப்பு கருதி இந்த நடவடிக்கை எடுக்கப்பட்டதாக வனத்துறை தெரிவித்துள்ளது' which is supported, but slides_spec says 'யானைகள் குட்டிகளுடன் அதிகம் நடமாடுவதால் தடை' is accurate; however the reel_script omits the detail that the ban was announced via social media only as an announcement with the elephant cause, which is fine
  reel_script claims 'ஹிந்து மக்கள் கட்சியும் எதிர்ப்பு தெரிவித்துள்ளது' which is in the article, but the mix of Hindu Munnani and Hindu Makkal Katchi is not clearly distinguished and could be read as the same group
  caption omits that the forest officials said the ban was for non-local visitors only in a way consistent with the article, but caption describes the ban as affecting 'பக்தர்கள்' generally, contradicting the article's local-only permission
  reel_script omits the key fact that the Hindu groups submitted a petition to the sub-collector Ramakrishnasamy's office details are partially present; the reel_script does mention it, so no omission there, but the key fact that the ban is in place 'தற்போதைய சூழ்நிலை' is not mentioned
